// Conformance fixture for ta.adx (S-bead OpenBBTechnical-0e9.5.26, Wave 5B-2).
//
// Author-derivative posture per PRD §7.3: reference output computed
// deterministically by running this script against a hard-coded synthetic
// (close, high, low) series (see ta_adx.csv). No chart data is
// redistributed; the .csv is a pure function of this .pine.
//
// Signature deviation note: PyneCore's ``lib.ta`` has no standalone ``adx``
// primitive — only ``dmi(diLength, adxSmoothing)`` which returns the
// (+DI, -DI, ADX) triple. This fixture calls ``ta.dmi`` directly and
// plots the third element (the ADX component) so the reference numbers
// stay purely PyneCore-derivative. The ``ta.adx`` bridge in
// ``openbb_pine.stdlib.ta`` synthesises exactly this: ``dmi(...)[2]``.
//
// Warm-up: ADX requires ``dilen`` bars for the +DI/-DI channels plus
// another ``adxlen`` bars for the RMA smoothing on top — so first ADX
// value appears at bar (dilen + adxlen - 1) at the earliest.
//@version=6
indicator("smoke_ta_adx", overlay=false)
[_dip, _dim, adx_val] = ta.dmi(5, 5)
plot(adx_val, title="adx5")
